    "https://www.quincy.edu/academics/career-preparation/": {
      "title": "Career Preparation",
      "description": "Career Preparation - Quincy University Skip To Main Content News Events Directory Info For... Close Menu Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Members Apply Visit Support QU Menu Toggle Search Close Main Menu About Back About Quincy University Success by Design Mission and Vision Catholic and Franciscan Identity Facts and Figures History Leadership Work at QU Contact Us Academics Back Academics All Degree Programs Graduate and Doctoral Degrees President’s Honors College Continuing Education Learning By Doing Career Preparation Academic Support Brenner Library Costs & Aid Back Costs & Aid Estimate Your Costs Tuition, Costs & Fees Scholarships Federal and State Aid Work Study Illinois Tuition Promise Program Admissions Back Admissions How to Apply Visit QU Request Information Admitted Students New Student Orientation Life at QU Back Life at QU Housing and Dining Clubs and Activities Traditions and Lore Faith and Ministry Health and Wellness Campus Safety About Our Town Athletics Apply Visit Support QU Info For Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Members News Events Directory Search Submit Search Home Academics Career Preparation Career Preparation In This Section In This Section Academic Support All Degree Programs Graduate and Doctoral Degrees President’s Honors College Continuing Education Learning By Doing Career Preparation Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Skill Development Courses Academic Support Brenner Library From classroom to career—and beyond. The QUEST Center at Quincy University is the university’s hub for career development and experiential learning. It supports students as they move from college to career by offering guidance, resources, and hands-on opportunities that connect academic learning with real-world experience. Through the QUEST Center, students receive help with career planning, résumés, interviews, and networking, while also gaining access to internships, practicums, and job opportunities. The center also coordinates experiential learning initiatives—such as service-learning, study abroad, undergraduate research, and credit for prior learning—in collaboration with faculty, staff, and community partners. Rooted in Quincy’s Franciscan tradition, the QUEST Center emphasizes reflection, relationships, and purposeful learning. Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Career Skill Courses 91% of graduates are employed in a professional position or in graduate school within six months of graduation. Kristen Liesen, Director of Experiential Learning Job Opportunities Students and Alumni Handshake is Quincy University’s career platform, connecting students with internships, part-time jobs, and full-time employment opportunities across a wide range of fields and locations. The platform provides personalized job recommendations based on your major and interests and offers opportunities to connect with fellow students, alumni, and employers. Your Quincy University information is preloaded in Handshake, making it easy to get started right away. To access your account, visit quincy.joinhandshake.com and login using your QU credentials. Employers Quincy University students bring talent, dedication, and fresh perspectives to today’s workforce. We welcome employers who are interested in connecting with motivated students and building meaningful partnerships that support both student success and organizational growth. There are several ways to engage with Quincy University. Handshake serves as the primary platform connecting employers with QU students and alumni across a wide range of academic backgrounds. Through internships, part-time roles, and full-time positions, employers can reach emerging professionals who are ready to learn and contribute. Employers may post opportunities directly in Handshake or email job descriptions and application instructions to Kristen Liesen. Organizations are also invited to visit campus to recruit at a table, offering the opportunity to meet students, share career opportunities, and build relationships in person. Through career preparation experiences such as mock interviews, networking events, and etiquette dinners, Quincy University students are well prepared to engage professionally with employers. Post-Graduation Outcomes This data reflects professional employment and graduate school outcomes for Quincy University undergraduate students in the graduating Class of 2024–2025. Outcome information was collected by the Director of Experiential Learning within six months of graduation. Post Graduation Outcomes Contact QUEST Center Kristin Liesen, Director of Experiential Learning 217-228-5432 extension 3355 [email protected] Kristen Liesen, MA Director of Experiential Learning TikTok LinkedIn Facebook Instagram X (Formerly known as Twitter) YouTube About Academics Costs & Aid Admissions Life at QU Athletics For Hawks myQuincy Portal Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Brenner Library Campus Map Location 1800 College Ave Quincy, IL 62301-2699 217-222-8020 Contact Us ©\n      2026\n      Quincy University Accreditation Accessibility Consumer Information Privacy Policy Title IX"
    },
    "https://www.quincy.edu/about/work-at-qu/job-openings/": {
      "title": "Job Openings",
      "description": "Job Openings - Quincy University Skip To Main Content News Events Directory Info For... Close Menu Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Members Apply Visit Support QU Menu Toggle Search Close Main Menu About Back About Quincy University Success by Design Mission and Vision Catholic and Franciscan Identity Facts and Figures History Leadership Work at QU Contact Us Academics Back Academics All Degree Programs Graduate and Doctoral Degrees President’s Honors College Continuing Education Learning By Doing Career Preparation Academic Support Brenner Library Costs & Aid Back Costs & Aid Estimate Your Costs Tuition, Costs & Fees Scholarships Federal and State Aid Work Study Illinois Tuition Promise Program Admissions Back Admissions How to Apply Visit QU Request Information Admitted Students New Student Orientation Life at QU Back Life at QU Housing and Dining Clubs and Activities Traditions and Lore Faith and Ministry Health and Wellness Campus Safety About Our Town Athletics Apply Visit Support QU Info For Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Members News Events Directory Search Submit Search Home About Work at QU Job Openings Job Openings In This Section In This Section Work at QU Benefits Job Openings Labor Law Information Human Resources Holiday Schedule Available Positions Explore current employment opportunities at Quincy University and discover how your talents can contribute to a mission-driven academic community. This page provides links to available faculty, staff, and administrative positions across the University. We invite you to review our openings and consider joining a campus dedicated to learning, service, and the holistic development of our students. Faculty Openings Non-Faculty Openings Graduate Assistant Openings Faculty Openings Full -Time Faculty positions in English Quincy University, a Catholic, Franciscan, and liberal arts institution emphasizing the development of servant leaders, invites applications for two tenure-track faculty positions in English at the rank of assistant professor or associate professor, beginning Fall 2027. Responsibilities: QU is seeking qualified candidates to teach courses in Composition, its co-requisite one-credit Writing Studio, literature, creative and technical writing, and related fields. The usual teaching load is 4 courses each semester. Academic advising and committee work are expected after the first year. The successful applicants for these positions will work cooperatively with colleagues in disciplines representing the liberal arts and the professions. Collaboration with faculty in Quincy University’s Communication program will be an expectation of our new faculty colleagues in English. Both disciplines are housed in the School of Fine Arts & Communication. Quincy University is committed to its English major and to advanced undergraduate instruction in the discipline. The successful applicants will play essential roles building enrollments through redesign of the English major. Qualifications: Specialties in any area of literature or writing are welcome. Applicants with expertise in one or more of the following areas are especially encouraged: (1) Catholic literature, including the Catholic literary canon; (2) rhetoric and composition, including business and administrative communication and science communication; (3) literature of the American Midwest. A doctoral degree in English, or a related field, with college-level teaching is preferred. Candidates with at least a Master’s degree in English, or a related field, may qualify for hire with the conversion of the position to non-tenure track. Position Start Date: August 16, 2027. Application Deadline : Review of applications will begin on September 15, 2026, and continue until the positions are filled. Salary: $50,000-$59,000, depending on experience. Benefits: We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes health, dental, and vision insurance; Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA); life insurance; long-term and short-term disability coverage; paid vacation, sick days, and holidays; parental leave; a 403(b) retirement plan; and tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Application Procedure: Send a letter of application, C.V., teaching philosophy, writing sample, example of teaching evaluations, copy of unofficial transcripts (must show all coursework completed and the conferral date of the degree), and contact information for three references to: Dr. Christine Damm Dean, School of Fine Arts & Communication c/o Office of Human Resources Quincy University 1800 College Ave. Quincy, IL 62301 or [email protected] Quincy University: Founded in 1860 by Franciscan friars, Quincy University is a Catholic university emphasizing the sciences, liberal arts and the professions. Quincy University offers 46 undergraduate programs, five master’s degrees, and a doctoral degree in Occupational Therapy, with a doctoral degree in Physical Therapy awaiting candidacy. QU is organized into six schools, the School of Fine Arts and Communication, the Oakley School of Business, the School of Humanities, the School of Education & Human Services, the School of Science and Technology, and the President’s Honors College. Quincy University invites submissions from all qualified applicants. Individuals who have earned degrees or taught at Catholic institutions or have other experiences of working with Catholic organizations recognized by the Church and aligning with Quincy University’s mission, are especially encouraged to apply. Whether Catholic or not, the successful applicant must be able to support the Catholic and Franciscan mission of Quincy University. For more information see Ex corde Ecclesiae, the Church’s Apostolic Constitution for Catholic universities. Faculty and advisors work with students to design customized success plans to help them graduate on time, find their passion and prepare them for life. QU is a member of NCAA Division II for intercollegiate athletics. For more information, please visit www.quincy.edu. Quincy University. Success by Design. It’s a great day to be a Hawk! Quincy, Illinois: Located in a tri-state area (Illinois, Missouri, and Iowa) on the banks of the Mississippi River, Quincy, Illinois is an affordable, family-friendly city of 40,000 residents with much to see and do! Quincy is rich in history, architecture, and cultural and recreational opportunities. St. Louis, MO is just over a 2-hour drive from Quincy. Kansas City, MO is 3 ½ hours and Quincy is 5 hours from Chicago by car. Quincy is also serviced by the Quincy Regional Airport and an Amtrak station. Employment Authorization : Employment is contingent upon a clear criminal background check. In compliance with federal law, all persons at the time of their start date will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. Instructor/Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice Quincy University, a Franciscan, Catholic, and liberal arts institution emphasizing the development of servant-leaders, seeks applicants for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Criminal Justice. Criminal Justice is one of the top five enrollments by major at QU. The University has an active mock-trial program, and other avenues for student involvement with the discipline such as the Women in Law club, as well as numerous internship and service opportunities. Responsibilities: QU is seeking qualified candidates to teach courses such as Foundations of Criminal Law, Contemporary Criminal Law and Procedure, Ethics, Justice, Diversity, Juvenile Delinquency, and/or other courses in their areas of expertise and interest. The usual teaching load is 4 courses each semester. Academic advising and committee work are expected after the first year. Qualifications: A doctorate in Criminal Justice, Law, or related field is required. Teaching experience at the college level is preferred. Position Start Date: August 17, 2026. Position Salary Range: $53,000 – $59,000 Benefits: We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes health, dental, and vision insurance; Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA); life insurance; long-term and short-term disability coverage; paid vacation, sick days, and holidays; parental leave; a 403(b)-retirement plan; and tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin June 1, 2026. The position will remain open until filled. Application Procedure: Applicants should submit a letter of application, statement of teaching philosophy, C.V, and contact information for three references to: Dr. Ken Oliver, Dean School of Education & Human Services c/o Office of Human Resources Quincy University 1800 College Avenue Quincy, IL 62301 or [email protected] Quincy University: QU serves nearly 1,200 full-time students and is growing! Founded in 1860 by Franciscan friars, Quincy University is a Catholic university emphasizing the sciences, liberal arts and the professions. Quincy University offers 46 undergraduate programs, five Master’s degrees, and two new Doctoral degrees in Physical Therapy and Occupational Therapy, integrating practical experience and Franciscan values. QU is organized into six schools, the School of Fine Arts and Communication, the Oakley School of Business, the School of Humanities, the School of Education & Human Services, the School of Science and Technology, and the President’s Honors College. Faculty and advisors work with students to design customized success plans to help them graduate on time, find their passion and prepare them for life. QU is a member of NCAA Division II for intercollegiate athletics. For more information, please visit www.quincy.edu. Quincy University. Success by Design. It’s a great day to be a Hawk! Quincy, Illinois: Located in a tri-state area (Illinois, Missouri, and Iowa) on the banks of the Mississippi River, Quincy, Illinois is an affordable, family-friendly city of 40,000 residents with much to see and do! Rich in history, Quincy was the site of the 6th Senatorial debate between Senator Stephen A. Douglas and his challenger, Abraham Lincoln. The architecture of Quincy spans pre-civil war through modern day. The Quincy Park District is made up of 1,000 acres divided into 26 parks, with many connections via an extensive network of hiking and biking trails. Quincy’s arts and culture scene boasts the Quincy Symphony Orchestra, Symphony Chorus, Youth Orchestra, Youth Chorus, the Quincy Community Theatre, and Arts Quincy, the first community arts council in the nation! St. Louis, MO is just over a 2 hour drive from Quincy. Kansas City, MO is 3 ½ hours and Quincy is five hours from Chicago by car. Quincy is also serviced by the Quincy Regional Airport and has an Amtrak station. Employment Authorization: Employment is contingent upon a clear criminal background check. In compliance with federal law, all persons at the time of their start date will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. An Equal Opportunity Employer Non-Faculty Openings Quincy University Security Officer The Safety & Security Department, a 24-7 operation has an immediate opening for fulltime Security Officer. Position requires sound judgement, effective communications skills, ability to walk for extended periods of time and work effectively with college age students. Previous law enforcement or security experience is preferred but not required. Responsibilities: • Serves as a representative of the University • Monitor campus door/camera security system • Unlock/lock buildings • Patrol campus perimeter • Monitor building and grounds for hazardous conditions • Make student, staff & faculty ID cards • Complete written reports • Complete other duties as assigned Qualifications: • At least 21 years of age • Valid driver’s license from the state he or she resides in • High school diploma or equivalent • Available for all shifts/flexibility in scheduling • Basic computer skills • Successful completion of background check Salary: $17.00 Benefits: We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes health, dental, and vision insurance; Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA); life insurance; long-term and short-term disability coverage; paid vacation, sick days, and holidays; parental leave; a 403(b) retirement plan; and tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Submit letter of application, resume and three references to: Robert Copley, Director of Safety & Security c/o Human Resources Quincy University 1800 College Ave. Quincy, IL 62301 or [email protected] An Equal Opportunity Employer Student Financial Services Counselor Quincy University seeks qualified applicants for a full-time Student Financial Services Counselor. Responsibilities: Serving as a counselor and advisor to students and their families as they consider options to finance a Quincy University education. One is expected to understand all federal, state, and University funding options. Student Financial Services counselors are expected to assist students with understanding and filing the Free Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA), explain the awarding process and ensure financial aid awards are delivered timely and accurately. All members of the staff are expected to develop expertise required to provide assistance in all areas of office operations. Counselors provide counseling in area of loan default prevention and financial literacy, responsible for loan origination and reconciliation, ensure awarded loans meet federal requirements and timely delivery of funds to students. Qualifications: While a Bachelor’s degree is preferred, an Associate’s degree is required with two or three years of experience in a financial aid office are required for consideration. Positive attitude Excellent written/verbal communication skills with the ability to provide timely and accurate information. Applicant must be detail-oriented and computer literate. Must pass federal financial aid officer training program (online). Salary: $17.00 hr Benefits: Includes medical, dental, vision, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, long- and short-term disability coverage, paid holidays, 403(b) retirement plan, tuition remission for undergraduate tuition for employees and dependents and graduate tuition for employees, as well as vacation and sick leave benefits in accordance with university policy. Send letter of application, resume and three professional references to: Tom Oliver, VP for Enrollment and Sr. Director of Student Financial Services c/o Office of Human Resources Quincy University 1800 College Ave. Quincy, IL  62301 or [email protected] An Equal Opportunity Employer Assistant Softball Coach Quincy University, a NCAA Division II institution and member of the Great Lakes Valley Conference, invites applications for the position of Assistant Softball Coach. Responsibilities: • Serves as a representative of the University, promoting QU’s mission, image and goals to colleagues and the community. • All aspects of recruitment including – scouting perspective student athletes, organizing staff recruiting calendar schedules, and the coordination of on campus recruit visits. • Assists in coaching, and training student athletes • Assist and coordinate with camp & clinics • Assist in field and facility maintenance • Perform other duties assigned by the Head Coach Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred. • Prior coaching or playing experience preferred. • Valid driver’s license with good driving record • Strong communication, leadership, and organizational skills Salary: $30,000 – $33,000 depending on experience Benefits: We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes health, dental, and vision insurance; Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA); life insurance; long-term and short-term disability coverage; paid vacation, sick days, and holidays; parental leave; a 403(b) retirement plan; and tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Send letter of application, resume and three professional references to: McKendree Ward, Head Softball Coach c/o Office of Human Resources Quincy University 1800 College Ave. Quincy, IL 62301 or [email protected] . An Equal Opportunity Employer Assistant Women’s Lacrosse Coach Quincy University, A NCAA Division II institution and member of the Great Lakes Valley Conference, invites applications for the position of Assistant-Women’s Lacrosse Coach Responsibilities: • Serves as a representative of the University, displaying courtesy, tact, consideration, and discretion in all interactions with the members of the QU community and with the public. • All aspects of recruitment including – scouting perspective student athletes, organizing staff recruiting calendar schedules, and the coordination of on campus recruit visits. • Assists in coaching, and training student athletes • Assist and coordinate with camp & clinics • Perform other duties assigned by the Head Coach Requirements: • Bachelor’s Degree • Playing experience and/or coaching experience at the collegiate level • Strong written and oral communication skills. • Ability to work with diverse student populations. • Flexible working hours (nights and weekends). Salary: $26,000–$28,000 Benefits: Includes medical, dental, vision, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, long- and short-term disability coverage, paid holidays, a 403(b) retirement plan, undergraduate tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents, graduate tuition benefits for employees, and vacation and sick leave in accordance with University policy. Send letter of application, resume, and three professional references to: Miles Stading, Head Women’s Lacrosse Coach C/O Office of Human Resources Quincy University 1800 College Ave. Quincy, II 62301 or [email protected] An Equal Opportunity Employer Seasonal Sprint Football Position Coach (Part-Time/Stipend Position) Quincy University is seeking a motivated and energetic Seasonal Sprint Football Position Coach to assist with the development and instruction of student-athletes within the Sprint Football program. This part-time, stipend position will work directly with a designated position group and support the overall mission of Quincy University Athletics. Responsibilities Include: • Coach and develop student-athletes within an assigned position group. • Assist with practice planning, drills, and game preparation. • Teach position-specific skills, techniques, and strategies. • Support student-athlete development both on and off the field. • Assist with recruiting efforts as assigned. • Participate in game-day operations and team activities. • Comply with all University, conference, league, and athletics department policies and procedures. • Perform other duties as assigned by the Head Coach. Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree preferred. • Previous football coaching and/or playing experience preferred. • Strong communication and leadership skills. • Valid driver’s license required. • Ability to work evening, weekends Salary: $6,000 Benefits: This position is not eligible for University benefits. Send letter of application, resume and three professional references to: Kirkland Burton, Head Sprint Football Coach c/o Office of Human Resources Quincy University 1800 College Ave. Quincy, IL 62301 or [email protected] An Equal Opportunity Employer Graduate Assistant Openings Graduate Assistant – Sprint Football Quincy University, a Catholic liberal arts university the Franciscan tradition, seeks qualified applicants for a Graduate Assistant- Sprint Football Coach Responsibilities: • Serves as a representative of the University, displaying courtesy, tact, consideration, and discretion in all interactions with the members of the QU community and with the public. • Assists the Head Coach with training, coaching, scouting and recruitment of student-athletes. • Assist and coordinate with camp & clinics • Perform other duties assigned by the Head Coach Requirements: • Bachelor’s Degree • Enrolled in Quincy University Master’s Program. • Strong written and oral communication skills. • Ability to work with diverse student populations. • Flexible working hours (nights and weekends). Send letter of application, resume, and three professional references to: Kirkland Burton, Head Sprint Football Coach c/o Office of Human Resources Quincy University 1800 College Ave. Quincy, IL 62301 or [email protected] An Equal Opportunity Employer Graduate Assistant- Freshman Student Assistant Quincy University seeks qualified applicants for the position of Graduate Assistant- Freshman Student Assistant Essential Functions/Responsibilities: Serves as a representative of the University, displaying courtesy, tact, consideration and discretion in all interactions with other members of the QU community and with the public. Assist Admissions Counselors in maintaining personal, written, and telephone communications with inquired and prospective students. Develop outreach strategies with the Dean of Admissions and Associate Deans of Admissions to optimize targeted communications Learn tour routes for undergraduate and graduate students and offer student tours upon request Assist Admissions Office Manager & Database Coordinator/Records Manager with data entry as needed Attend and assist with all Admissions on-campus event days Other duties as assigned Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Valid Driver’s License Apply and be accepted into the graduate program at Quincy University One year’s experience of working within a customer-focused environment Experience with student recruitment and/or marketing preferred Familiarity and/or practice of tele-marketing communications Salary: $6,000 per academic year (August through May) Graduate Tuition Waiver: Up to 15 credit hours for MBA (prerequisites included) or 16 credit hours for MSE and MEC. Send letter of application, resume, and three professional references to: Justin Ray. Dean of Admissions c/o Office of Human Resources Quincy University 1800 College Ave. Quincy, IL 62301 Or [email protected] An Equal Opportunity Employer Contact Human Resources Diane Kemner, Payroll/Benefit Coordinator Francis Hall, Room B38 217-222-8020, extension 3670 217-228-5323 (fax) [email protected] Diane Kemner Payroll/Benefit Coordinator TikTok LinkedIn Facebook Instagram X (Formerly known as Twitter) YouTube About Academics Costs & Aid Admissions Life at QU Athletics For Hawks myQuincy Portal Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Brenner Library Campus Map Location 1800 College Ave Quincy, IL 62301-2699 217-222-8020 Contact Us ©\n      2026\n      Quincy University Accreditation Accessibility Consumer Information Privacy Policy Title IX"
    }
